        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media): preserve UTF-16 surrogate pairs in live test helpers truncation",
        "body": "\"## Summary\\n\\nReplace `.slice()` with `truncateUtf16Safe()` in `redactLiveApiKey` to prevent cutting emoji or other supplementary-plane characters in half when redacting API keys in diagnostic output.\\n\\n## What Problem This Solves\\n\\n**Problem**: `redactLiveApiKey` used `String.prototype.slice()` at code-unit index boundaries (`.slice(0, 8)` and `.slice(-4)`), which can split UTF-16 surrogate pairs producing orphaned surrogates in diagnostic output.\\n\\n**Root Cause**: The function in `src/media-generation/live-test-helpers.ts:24` uses raw `.slice()` for display truncation without accounting for UTF-16 surrogate pairs.\\n\\n**Solution**: Replace `.slice(0, 8)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(trimmed, 8)` and `.slice(-4)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(trimmed.slice(-4), 4)`, which adjust the boundary away from surrogate pair splits.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n**Real environment tested**: Linux 6.17.0-35-generic, Node.js v25.9.0\\n\\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\\n```bash\\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/media-generation/live-test-helpers.test.ts\\n```\\n\\n```\\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\\n```\\n\\nThe \\\"preserves UTF-16 surrogate pairs\\\" test uses a key `\\\"abcdefg\\ud83d\\ude00hijklmnop\\\"` where the emoji sits at code-unit positions 7-8. Raw `.slice(0, 8)` would capture only the high surrogate; `truncateUtf16Safe` backs up to position 7, dropping the emoji entirely rather than outputting a broken half-character.\\n\\n**What was not tested**: No UI-level integration test. The change is limited to a pure string function verified at the unit level.\\n\\n## Tests and validation\\n\\n- 7/7 tests passed in `live-test-helpers.test.ts` including emoji boundary preservation test\\n\\n## Risk checklist\\n\\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation\\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary\\n\\nmerge-risk: low\\n\"",
